://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-13T15:50:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T18:49:53Z","body":"I think the problem is that I modified `Label::get_minimum_size` to automatically expand when it has a maximum size, which was, looking back, not the right approach. The problem I encountered with it is that a `Label` cannot be shrunk in that case, which isn't just an issue for this, but also usability. I have a fix for that. I'll see if it fixes this issue, too. \nI'm still working on it, but I have a proper solution in the works. \n\nEdit: nope, that's not it, bruvzg is likely right","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4237762335/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4237793445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118501#issuecomment-4237793445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118501","id":4237793445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78l5il","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://av